                "senderName": "NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 2 at 8:36AM CDT until September 2 at 12:30PM CDT by NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "description": "FFWLCH\n\nThe National Weather Service in Lake Charles has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nHardin County in southeastern Texas...\nCentral Jasper County in southeastern Texas...\nTyler County in southeastern Texas...\n\n* Until 1230 PM CDT.\n\n* At 836 AM CDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain in Reports of flood have been received from Tyler and\nHardin Counties. Between 5 and 20 inches of rain have fallen. The\nexpected rainfall rate is 1 to 4 inches in 1 hour. Additional\nrainfall amounts of 1 to 5 inches are possible in the warned area.\nFlash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLumberton, Silsbee, Woodville, Kountze, Sour Lake, Colmesneil,\nChester, Wildwood, Warren, Fred, Thicket, Saratoga, Town Bluff,\nVillage Mills, Honey Island, Caney Head, Spurger, Votaw and Batson.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
