                "description": "FFWLCH\n\nThe National Weather Service in Lake Charles has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCentral Hardin County in southeastern Texas...\nSouth Central Tyler County in southeastern Texas...\n\n* Until 1045 AM CDT.\n\n* At 546 AM CDT, emergency management reported thunderstorms\nproducing heavy rain across the warned area. Between 10 and 21\ninches of rain have fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1 to 5\ninches in 1 hour. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nFLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY for Kountze, Village Mills, Honey Island.\nThis is a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER GROUND NOW!\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...This is a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER\nGROUND NOW! Life threatening flash flooding of low water\ncrossings, small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLumberton, Kountze, Wildwood, Saratoga, Warren, Honey Island,\nVillage Mills and Batson.\n\nDown stream locations such as Village Creek State Park and low areas\nbetween Silsbee and Lumberton.",
